   "text": "RAG basics",
   "originalText": "RAG basics",
   "fontSize": 24,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "g1_body",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 54,
   "y": 2588,
   "width": 572.88,
   "height": 770.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#3d3d3d",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1357122901,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 311583110,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "RAG: Retrieval-Augmented Generation: first find relevant passages,\n   then let an LLM answer using only them, so answers are grounded\n   and citable.\n\nLLM: Large Language Model, e.g. gpt-oss-120b or Qwen. Generates\n   text.\n\nRBAC: Role-Based Access Control: what you may see depends on your\n   role (engineering, hr, finance...).\n\nRole / c_level: The user's job group. c_level = executives (CEO,\n   CFO), who see everything.\n\nallowed_roles: List stored on each document/chunk naming the roles\n   that may see it.\n\nCorpus: The full set of documents the chatbot can search (here\n   275).\n\nManifest: Our index file (manifest.jsonl): one line per document\n   with id, path, URL, licence, hash and allowed_roles.\n\nIngestion / indexing: Turning raw files into searchable chunks in\n   the database.\n\nDocling: Open-source tool that converts PDF/DOCX/XLSX into\n   structured text with headings and tables.\n\nChunk: A small piece of a document (~512 tokens) that gets\n   searched and cited.\n\nToken: The unit LLMs read; roughly 3/4 of a word.\n\nEmbedding: A list of numbers (vector) capturing a text's meaning;\n   similar meaning = nearby vectors.\n\nVector DB / Qdrant: Database that stores embeddings and finds the\n   nearest ones fast. Qdrant is the one we plan to use.\n\nCitation: A pointer from an answer sentence to the chunk that\n   supports it.\n\nHallucination: An LLM stating something not supported by its\n   sources.",
   "originalText": "RAG: Retrieval-Augmented Generation: first find relevant passages,\n   then let an LLM answer using only them, so answers are grounded\n   and citable.\n\nLLM: Large Language Model, e.g. gpt-oss-120b or Qwen. Generates\n   text.\n\nRBAC: Role-Based Access Control: what you may see depends on your\n   role (engineering, hr, finance...).\n\nRole / c_level: The user's job group. c_level = executives (CEO,\n   CFO), who see everything.\n\nallowed_roles: List stored on each document/chunk naming the roles\n   that may see it.\n\nCorpus: The full set of documents the chatbot can search (here\n   275).\n\nManifest: Our index file (manifest.jsonl): one line per document\n   with id, path, URL, licence, hash and allowed_roles.\n\nIngestion / indexing: Turning raw files into searchable chunks in\n   the database.\n\nDocling: Open-source tool that converts PDF/DOCX/XLSX into\n   structured text with headings and tables.\n\nChunk: A small piece of a document (~512 tokens) that gets\n   searched and cited.\n\nToken: The unit LLMs read; roughly 3/4 of a word.\n\nEmbedding: A list of numbers (vector) capturing a text's meaning;\n   similar meaning = nearby vectors.\n\nVector DB / Qdrant: Database that stores embeddings and finds the\n   nearest ones fast. Qdrant is the one we plan to use.\n\nCitation: A pointer from an answer sentence to the chunk that\n   supports it.\n\nHallucination: An LLM stating something not supported by its\n   sources.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
