   "locked": false,
   "text": "Search and ranking",
   "originalText": "Search and ranking",
   "fontSize": 24,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
  {
   "id": "g2_body",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 774,
   "y": 2588,
   "width": 572.88,
   "height": 612.5,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#3d3d3d",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 1,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 1300430509,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 525488742,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": [],
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Retrieval: Finding the chunks most relevant to a question.\n\nDense retrieval: Search by meaning, using embeddings. Catches\n   paraphrases.\n\nSparse retrieval / BM25: Classic keyword search scoring (Best\n   Match 25). Catches exact words, codes, IDs.\n\nHybrid search: Running dense + sparse together and merging the\n   results.\n\nRRF: Reciprocal Rank Fusion: merges ranked lists by adding 1/(60 +\n   rank) per list. Needs no score tuning.\n\nReranker / cross-encoder: A second, slower model that reads\n   question + chunk together and re-orders the top 50-100\n   candidates.\n\nTop-k: The k best results kept (e.g. top-5, top-10).\n\nPre-filter vs post-filter: Pre = remove forbidden docs inside the\n   search itself (safe). Post = remove them after (can leak and\n   starve results). We use pre.\n\nReference retriever: Our simple BM25 search over whole documents,\n   used only to test the eval harness. Not the real chatbot.\n\nAblation: An experiment that changes one thing (e.g. add reranker)\n   and measures the effect.\n\nChunking strategy: How documents are cut: fixed size, by headings,\n   overlap between pieces, parent/child.\n\nOverlap: Repeating a few sentences between neighbouring chunks so\n   ideas aren't cut in half.",
   "originalText": "Retrieval: Finding the chunks most relevant to a question.\n\nDense retrieval: Search by meaning, using embeddings. Catches\n   paraphrases.\n\nSparse retrieval / BM25: Classic keyword search scoring (Best\n   Match 25). Catches exact words, codes, IDs.\n\nHybrid search: Running dense + sparse together and merging the\n   results.\n\nRRF: Reciprocal Rank Fusion: merges ranked lists by adding 1/(60 +\n   rank) per list. Needs no score tuning.\n\nReranker / cross-encoder: A second, slower model that reads\n   question + chunk together and re-orders the top 50-100\n   candidates.\n\nTop-k: The k best results kept (e.g. top-5, top-10).\n\nPre-filter vs post-filter: Pre = remove forbidden docs inside the\n   search itself (safe). Post = remove them after (can leak and\n   starve results). We use pre.\n\nReference retriever: Our simple BM25 search over whole documents,\n   used only to test the eval harness. Not the real chatbot.\n\nAblation: An experiment that changes one thing (e.g. add reranker)\n   and measures the effect.\n\nChunking strategy: How documents are cut: fixed size, by headings,\n   overlap between pieces, parent/child.\n\nOverlap: Repeating a few sentences between neighbouring chunks so\n   ideas aren't cut in half.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
