   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Golden set: Our hand-checked list of test questions with correct\n   answers, sources and the asking role.\n\nGold evidence / quote: The exact sentence(s) in a document that\n   prove the answer. Used instead of chunk IDs so any chunking can\n   be scored.\n\nDev / test split: Dev questions are for tuning; test questions\n   only for reported numbers, so results aren't flattered.\n\nHarness: The program that runs every golden question through the\n   chatbot and scores it.\n\nhit@k / hit rate: Share of questions where a correct chunk is in\n   the top k results.\n\nRecall@k: Share of all needed evidence found in the top k.\n\nMRR: Mean Reciprocal Rank: 1/position of the first correct chunk,\n   averaged. 1.0 = always first.\n\nnDCG@10: normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain: ranking quality of\n   the top 10; correct items lower down count less.\n\nFaithfulness: Is every claim in the answer supported by the\n   retrieved text?\n\nAnswer relevancy: Does the answer actually address the question?\n\nCitation precision: Share of citations that really support their\n   sentence.\n\nLLM-as-judge: Using a strong LLM to grade answers. Must be checked\n   against human labels.\n\np50 / p95 latency: Typical (median) and slow-case (95th\n   percentile) response time.\n\n$/q: Cost in dollars per question (LLM tokens).",
   "originalText": "Golden set: Our hand-checked list of test questions with correct\n   answers, sources and the asking role.\n\nGold evidence / quote: The exact sentence(s) in a document that\n   prove the answer. Used instead of chunk IDs so any chunking can\n   be scored.\n\nDev / test split: Dev questions are for tuning; test questions\n   only for reported numbers, so results aren't flattered.\n\nHarness: The program that runs every golden question through the\n   chatbot and scores it.\n\nhit@k / hit rate: Share of questions where a correct chunk is in\n   the top k results.\n\nRecall@k: Share of all needed evidence found in the top k.\n\nMRR: Mean Reciprocal Rank: 1/position of the first correct chunk,\n   averaged. 1.0 = always first.\n\nnDCG@10: normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain: ranking quality of\n   the top 10; correct items lower down count less.\n\nFaithfulness: Is every claim in the answer supported by the\n   retrieved text?\n\nAnswer relevancy: Does the answer actually address the question?\n\nCitation precision: Share of citations that really support their\n   sentence.\n\nLLM-as-judge: Using a strong LLM to grade answers. Must be checked\n   against human labels.\n\np50 / p95 latency: Typical (median) and slow-case (95th\n   percentile) response time.\n\n$/q: Cost in dollars per question (LLM tokens).",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
