   "locked": false,
   "text": "GitLab Handbook: GitLab's public company handbook; our stand-in\n   for internal docs.\n\nPinned commit / SHA: An exact version of the handbook repo\n   (322e725a), so the sample never changes.\n\nSparse checkout: Downloading only some folders of a git repo\n   instead of all of it.\n\nFront matter: The settings block at the top of a handbook page\n   (title etc.).\n\nSEC / EDGAR: US Securities and Exchange Commission and its public\n   filings website.\n\n10-K / 10-Q: Annual report / quarterly report a listed company\n   must file.\n\nCIK / accession no.: EDGAR's company ID (GitLab = 1653482) / ID of\n   one filing.\n\niXBRL: Inline XBRL: HTML with machine-readable financial tags;\n   EDGAR's format.\n\nFY / Q1-Q4 / H1: Fiscal year (GitLab's runs Feb-Jan; FY2027 = Feb\n   2026-Jan 2027) / quarters / first half.\n\nOpex / plan vs actual / variance: Operating expenses / budgeted vs\n   real spend / the difference.\n\nHeadcount: Number of employees.\n\nSynthetic data: Made-up but realistic data generated by code.\n\nSeed: Fixed random number start (42) so generated data and samples\n   are reproducible.\n\nCC BY-SA 4.0 / CC BY-NC / MIT: Licences: share with credit + same\n   licence / credit, non-commercial only / free use with notice.\n\nFinanceBench: Public benchmark of finance Q&A (other companies);\n   optional, off.",
   "originalText": "GitLab Handbook: GitLab's public company handbook; our stand-in\n   for internal docs.\n\nPinned commit / SHA: An exact version of the handbook repo\n   (322e725a), so the sample never changes.\n\nSparse checkout: Downloading only some folders of a git repo\n   instead of all of it.\n\nFront matter: The settings block at the top of a handbook page\n   (title etc.).\n\nSEC / EDGAR: US Securities and Exchange Commission and its public\n   filings website.\n\n10-K / 10-Q: Annual report / quarterly report a listed company\n   must file.\n\nCIK / accession no.: EDGAR's company ID (GitLab = 1653482) / ID of\n   one filing.\n\niXBRL: Inline XBRL: HTML with machine-readable financial tags;\n   EDGAR's format.\n\nFY / Q1-Q4 / H1: Fiscal year (GitLab's runs Feb-Jan; FY2027 = Feb\n   2026-Jan 2027) / quarters / first half.\n\nOpex / plan vs actual / variance: Operating expenses / budgeted vs\n   real spend / the difference.\n\nHeadcount: Number of employees.\n\nSynthetic data: Made-up but realistic data generated by code.\n\nSeed: Fixed random number start (42) so generated data and samples\n   are reproducible.\n\nCC BY-SA 4.0 / CC BY-NC / MIT: Licences: share with credit + same\n   licence / credit, non-commercial only / free use with notice.\n\nFinanceBench: Public benchmark of finance Q&A (other companies);\n   optional, off.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
