   "text": "Groq: Fast LLM API provider. Our only key; free tier = 8,000\n   tokens/minute.\n\ngpt-oss-120b / qwen3.8-27b: Open-weight LLMs on Groq: drafting +\n   judging / answering.\n\nRate limit / HTTP 429: Max usage per minute / the error returned\n   when it's exceeded; we wait and retry.\n\nAPI key / .env: Secret password for an API / local file holding\n   it, kept out of git.\n\nDeepEval: Open-source library of LLM eval metrics (faithfulness\n   etc.).\n\nRAGAS: Similar eval library; an alternative to DeepEval.\n\nLangSmith / Langfuse: Tracing tools that record every step, timing\n   and cost of a request.\n\nuv / pytest / ruff: Python package manager / test runner / linter\n   (style + bug checker).\n\nPlaywright / Chromium: Headless browser we use to print the SEC\n   HTML to PDF.\n\nCI / GitHub Actions: Continuous Integration: tests and evals run\n   automatically on every push.\n\nTDD: Test-Driven Development: write the failing test first, then\n   the code.\n\nSpec / plan: The design document (what and why) / the step-by-step\n   build list (how).\n\nNative vs Subagent-driven: Build modes: I build everything in this\n   session, vs a fresh helper agent per task with reviews.\n\nSuperpowers: Skill set guiding the process: brainstorming,\n   writing-plans, TDD, verification.",
   "originalText": "Groq: Fast LLM API provider. Our only key; free tier = 8,000\n   tokens/minute.\n\ngpt-oss-120b / qwen3.8-27b: Open-weight LLMs on Groq: drafting +\n   judging / answering.\n\nRate limit / HTTP 429: Max usage per minute / the error returned\n   when it's exceeded; we wait and retry.\n\nAPI key / .env: Secret password for an API / local file holding\n   it, kept out of git.\n\nDeepEval: Open-source library of LLM eval metrics (faithfulness\n   etc.).\n\nRAGAS: Similar eval library; an alternative to DeepEval.\n\nLangSmith / Langfuse: Tracing tools that record every step, timing\n   and cost of a request.\n\nuv / pytest / ruff: Python package manager / test runner / linter\n   (style + bug checker).\n\nPlaywright / Chromium: Headless browser we use to print the SEC\n   HTML to PDF.\n\nCI / GitHub Actions: Continuous Integration: tests and evals run\n   automatically on every push.\n\nTDD: Test-Driven Development: write the failing test first, then\n   the code.\n\nSpec / plan: The design document (what and why) / the step-by-step\n   build list (how).\n\nNative vs Subagent-driven: Build modes: I build everything in this\n   session, vs a fresh helper agent per task with reviews.\n\nSuperpowers: Skill set guiding the process: brainstorming,\n   writing-plans, TDD, verification.",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
   "autoResize": true
  },
